    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\npagetitle: \"Licensing Synroc · SCPU3001\"\ndescription: \"Where ANSTO should take its Synroc waste technology next: an interactive summary of our SCPU3001 project.\"\n---\n\n```{=html}\n<script id=\"synroc-data\" type=\"application/json\">{\"countries\":[{\"id\":\"NL\",\"name\":\"Netherlands\",\"bloc\":\"EU\",\"stream\":\"Candidate\",\"stage1\":\"Proceeds\",\"legal\":3,\"political\":5,\"site\":\"Curium, Petten \\u00b7 COVRA, Nieuwdorp\",\"note\":\"Liquid waste from fission Mo-99. COVRA takes ownership at hand-over for a one-off charge and stores it until disposal, foreseen around 2130, so every cubic metre avoided saves the full charge.\",\"rq3\":4},{\"id\":\"BE\",\"name\":\"Belgium\",\"bloc\":\"EU\",\"stream\":\"Candidate\",\"stage1\":\"Proceeds\",\"legal\":3,\"political\":4,\"site\":\"IRE, Fleurus \\u00b7 ONDRAF / Belgoprocess, Dessel\",\"note\":\"Same process family as Petten; about 3.2 m\\u00b3 a year in 1985\\u201396. Uranium recovery (RECUMO) may change which stream remains.\",\"rq3\":3.5},{\"id\":\"ZA\",\"name\":\"South Africa\",\"bloc\":\"Commonwealth\",\"stream\":\"Needs data\",\"stage1\":\"Evidence gap\",\"legal\":3,\"political\":2,\"site\":\"NTP, Pelindaba\",\"note\":\"Same process family, but no volume data, a repository around 2065 and a regulator that halted production for about a year.\",\"rq3\":2.5},{\"id\":\"AU\",\"name\":\"Australia\",\"bloc\":\"Benchmark\",\"stream\":\"Benchmark\",\"stage1\":\"Benchmark\",\"legal\":4,\"political\":3,\"site\":\"ANSTO, Lucas Heights (SyMo)\",\"note\":\"ANSTO's own plant, SyMo, is being commissioned. The national waste site at Kimba was abandoned in 2023.\",\"rq3\":3.5},{\"id\":\"CA\",\"name\":\"Canada\",\"bloc\":\"Commonwealth\",\"stream\":\"No stream\",\"stage1\":\"Excluded\",\"legal\":3,\"political\":3,\"site\":\"Darlington (neutron capture)\",\"note\":\"Darlington's Mo-99 route leaves no comparable liquid waste, and the ILW repository is unsited, so avoided costs are decades away.\",\"rq3\":3},{\"id\":\"UK\",\"name\":\"United Kingdom\",\"bloc\":\"Commonwealth\",\"stream\":\"No stream\",\"stage1\":\"Excluded\",\"legal\":4,\"political\":4,\"site\":\"Resins and sludges only\",\"note\":\"The only regulator with a staged process to assess a new wasteform before a repository exists, but no isotope waste stream.\",\"rq3\":4},{\"id\":\"FR\",\"name\":\"France\",\"bloc\":\"EU\",\"stream\":\"No stream\",\"stage1\":\"Excluded\",\"legal\":3,\"political\":2,\"site\":\"No current producer\",\"note\":\"Backs its own vitrification industry (La Hague); no current Mo-99 producer.\",\"rq3\":2.5},{\"id\":\"NZ\",\"name\":\"New Zealand\",\"bloc\":\"Commonwealth\",\"stream\":\"No stream\",\"stage1\":\"Excluded\",\"legal\":1,\"political\":1,\"site\":\"No candidate stream\",\"note\":\"No licence route and a nuclear-free identity; no isotope waste stream.\",\"rq3\":1}],\"scores\":[{\"id\":\"NL\",\"rq1\":3,\"rq2\":5,\"rq3\":4,\"rq4\":3},{\"id\":\"BE\",\"rq1\":2,\"rq2\":4,\"rq3\":3.5,\"rq4\":3},{\"id\":\"ZA\",\"rq1\":3,\"rq2\":null,\"rq3\":2.5,\"rq4\":3}],\"smaa\":{\"NL\":1,\"BE\":0},\"n_draws\":10000,\"econ\":[{\"id\":\"NL\",\"name\":\"Netherlands (COVRA)\",\"saving_per_m3\":2.7,\"breakeven\":0.5,\"volume\":0.7,\"p_cheaper\":0.96},{\"id\":\"BE\",\"name\":\"Belgium (ONDRAF)\",\"saving_per_m3\":1.4,\"breakeven\":1,\"volume\":3.2,\"p_cheaper\":0.81}],\"risks\":[{\"id\":\"R1\",\"risk\":\"Agency declines to adopt Synroc or re-prices its product\",\"L\":3,\"I\":3,\"RL\":2,\"RI\":3,\"response\":\"Approach agencies as licensees; acceptance and tariff as licence conditions (G2)\"},{\"id\":\"R2\",\"risk\":\"Saving does not reach the payer\",\"L\":3,\"I\":2,\"RL\":2,\"RI\":2,\"response\":\"Savings-share licence priced on the agency's avoided cost\"},{\"id\":\"R3\",\"risk\":\"Dutch volume unverified or below break-even\",\"L\":2,\"I\":3,\"RL\":2,\"RI\":3,\"response\":\"Measure the volume during characterisation (G1)\"},{\"id\":\"R4\",\"risk\":\"Non-reactor Mo-99 displaces fission output\",\"L\":2,\"I\":3,\"RL\":2,\"RI\":3,\"response\":\"Monitor; minimum annual payment\"},{\"id\":\"R5\",\"risk\":\"RECUMO removes or relocates IRE's liquid ILW\",\"L\":2,\"I\":3,\"RL\":2,\"RI\":3,\"response\":\"Characterise RECUMO residues within G1\"},{\"id\":\"R6\",\"risk\":\"No operating reference plant\",\"L\":3,\"I\":3,\"RL\":3,\"RI\":3,\"response\":\"Sign only after the ARPANSA operating licence (G3)\"},{\"id\":\"R7\",\"risk\":\"Shared formulation fails on licensee waste\",\"L\":2,\"I\":3,\"RL\":1,\"RI\":3,\"response\":\"Simulant trials; re-tailor the formulation (G1)\"},{\"id\":\"R8\",\"risk\":\"Licensee first-plant cost overrun\",\"L\":2,\"I\":3,\"RL\":2,\"RI\":2,\"response\":\"Reuse existing cells; fixed-price engineering package\"},{\"id\":\"R9\",\"risk\":\"Repository programmes slip\",\"L\":3,\"I\":1,\"RL\":3,\"RI\":1,\"response\":\"Monitor\"},{\"id\":\"R10\",\"risk\":\"Service model blocked\",\"L\":3,\"I\":1,\"RL\":3,\"RI\":1,\"response\":\"None needed; licensing recommended\"},{\"id\":\"R11\",\"risk\":\"Technology-transfer conditions\",\"L\":1,\"I\":2,\"RL\":1,\"RI\":1,\"response\":\"Confirm scope early; local partner\"},{\"id\":\"R12\",\"risk\":\"Licensor warranty liability\",\"L\":2,\"I\":2,\"RL\":1,\"RI\":2,\"response\":\"Limit warranties to the G1-G2 specification\"},{\"id\":\"R13\",\"risk\":\"IP leakage to competing producers\",\"L\":2,\"I\":2,\"RL\":1,\"RI\":2,\"response\":\"License to agencies; staged know-how release\"},{\"id\":\"R14\",\"risk\":\"Revenue concentration\",\"L\":3,\"I\":2,\"RL\":3,\"RI\":1,\"response\":\"Upfront fee and minimum annual payment\"},{\"id\":\"R15\",\"risk\":\"Trust at Petten after 2025 enforcement\",\"L\":2,\"I\":2,\"RL\":2,\"RI\":2,\"response\":\"Engage COVRA and Curium before contracts\"},{\"id\":\"R16\",\"risk\":\"Trust at Fleurus after 2008 release\",\"L\":2,\"I\":2,\"RL\":2,\"RI\":2,\"response\":\"Engage before contracts; publish evidence\"}],\"discount_rate\":0.035}</script>\n```\n\n```{=html}\n<nav class=\"nav\">\n  <div class=\"nav-inner\">\n    <a class=\"brand\" href=\"#top\">Licensing <span>Synroc</span></a>\n    <div class=\"nav-links\">\n      <a href=\"#problem\">Problem</a>\n      <a href=\"#where\">Where</a>\n      <a href=\"#questions\">Research</a>\n      <a href=\"#decision\">Decision</a>\n      <a href=\"#economics\">Economics</a>\n      <a href=\"#risks\">Risks</a>\n      <a href=\"#plan\">Plan</a>\n      <a href=\"references.html\">Sources</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</nav>\n\n<!-- ============================== HERO ============================== -->\n<header class=\"section hero\" id=\"top\">\n  <span class=\"kicker\">SCPU3001 · Industry partner: ANSTO</span>\n  <h1>Licensing<br>Synroc</h1>\n  <p class=\"lede\">Every nuclear-medicine scan leaves radioactive waste behind. ANSTO can shrink it by up to 99%. Our question: <b>where should ANSTO take this technology first?</b></p>\n  <div class=\"hero-actions\">\n    <a class=\"cta solid\" href=\"#decision\">Try the decision model</a>\n    <a class=\"cta\" href=\"#plan\">See our plan</a>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"grid-4\">\n    <div class=\"panel stat reveal\"><div class=\"num\" data-count=\"99\" data-suffix=\"%\">99%</div><div class=\"lab\">less waste volume than cement, at best <a class=\"cite\" href=\"references.html#r2\">[2]</a></div></div>\n    <div class=\"panel stat reveal\"><div class=\"num\"><span data-count=\"2\">2</span> sites</div><div class=\"lab\">fit today: Petten (NL) and Fleurus (BE)</div></div>\n    <div class=\"panel stat reveal\"><div class=\"num\" data-count=\"100\" data-suffix=\"%\">100%</div><div class=\"lab\">of 10,000 weightings rank the Netherlands first</div></div>\n    <div class=\"panel stat reveal\"><div class=\"num\"><span data-count=\"3\">3</span> gates</div><div class=\"lab\">to pass before any licence is signed</div></div>\n  </div>\n  <p class=\"team-line\">Morris · Lydia · Ibrahim · Andres · Tommy · Delphine — University of Sydney, October 2026</p>\n</header>\n\n<!-- ============================ PROBLEM ============================= -->\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"problem\">\n  <span class=\"kicker\">01 · The problem</span>\n  <h2>Waste with nowhere to go,<br>a fix without a market</h2>\n  <p class=\"lede\">Making molybdenum-99 leaves 2.6–15 m³ of liquid radioactive waste a year worldwide <a class=\"cite\" href=\"references.html#r1\">[1]</a>, <a class=\"cite\" href=\"references.html#r3\">[3]</a>. No target country can dispose of it yet: the Netherlands plans disposal around 2130 <a class=\"cite\" href=\"references.html#r4\">[4]</a>. ANSTO's Synroc shrinks it, and its first plant, SyMo, is being commissioned <a class=\"cite\" href=\"references.html#r5\">[5]</a>.</p>\n  <div class=\"grid-2\" style=\"margin-top:28px\">\n    <div class=\"panel reveal\">\n      <h3>Shrink the waste</h3>\n      <p class=\"note\" style=\"margin-top:0\">Drag to set the liquid waste a producer makes each year. Cube sizes are drawn to true volume.</p>\n      <div class=\"control\">\n        <label for=\"vol\">Liquid waste per year <output id=\"volOut\">3.0 m³</output></label>\n        <input type=\"range\" id=\"vol\" min=\"0.5\" max=\"15\" step=\"0.1\" value=\"3\">\n      </div>\n      <svg class=\"cubes\" id=\"cubes\" viewBox=\"0 0 560 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Volume comparison cubes\"></svg>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"panel reveal\">\n      <h3>What changes</h3>\n      <div class=\"big-compare\">\n        <span class=\"pill pink\">Cemented: <b id=\"cemOut\">25 m³</b></span>\n        <span class=\"pill mint\">Synroc: <b id=\"synOut\">0.25–1 m³</b></span>\n      </div>\n      <p style=\"margin-top:18px\">Cemented, each cubic metre becomes about <b>25 m³</b> of packages that must be stored, and paid for, until disposal. Synroc turns it into <b>0.25–1 m³</b> of dense ceramic <a class=\"cite\" href=\"references.html#r2\">[2]</a>, <a class=\"cite\" href=\"references.html#r3\">[3]</a>.</p>\n      <p><b>Our aim:</b> show ANSTO where, and in what commercial form, to offer Synroc abroad.</p>\n      <h3 style=\"margin-top:22px\">Who gains if it works</h3>\n      <div class=\"grid-2\" style=\"gap:10px\">\n        <div class=\"pill mint\">ANSTO: export revenue, no plant abroad</div>\n        <div class=\"pill blue\">COVRA, ONDRAF: up to 99% less to store</div>\n        <div class=\"pill\" style=\"background:var(--lilac)\">Curium, IRE: lower waste charges</div>\n        <div class=\"pill pink\">Host towns: no new waste site</div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<!-- ============================= WHERE ============================== -->\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"where\">\n  <span class=\"kicker\">02 · Where the waste is</span>\n  <h2>Eight jurisdictions, two real candidates</h2>\n  <p class=\"lede\">We screened four Commonwealth and three EU countries against Australia as the benchmark. Click a country.</p>\n  <div class=\"legend\">\n    <span><i class=\"st-Proceeds\"></i>Proceeds to ranking</span>\n    <span><i class=\"st-Evidence\"></i>Evidence gap</span>\n    <span><i class=\"st-Benchmark\"></i>Benchmark</span>\n    <span><i class=\"st-Excluded\"></i>Excluded: no matching waste</span>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"chips\" id=\"chips\"></div>\n  <div class=\"panel detail reveal\" id=\"countryDetail\"></div>\n  <p class=\"note\">Legal score: four-question test of each jurisdiction's law. Political score: Kingdon's policy-window model <a class=\"cite\" href=\"references.html#r7\">[7]</a>. Both 1–5.</p>\n</section>\n\n<!-- =========================== QUESTIONS ============================ -->\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"questions\">\n  <span class=\"kicker\">03 · Four questions</span>\n  <h2>Four disciplines, one decision</h2>\n  <p class=\"lede\">Each of us took one question. Each answer is a condition a rollout must meet.</p>\n  <div class=\"tabs\" id=\"rqTabs\"></div>\n  <div class=\"rq-grid\" id=\"rqPanel\"></div>\n</section>\n\n<!-- ============================ DECISION ============================ -->\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"decision\">\n  <span class=\"kicker\">04 · The decision model</span>\n  <h2>Weigh it your way</h2>\n  <p class=\"lede\">Stage 1 screened out every site that fails a must-have. Stage 2 ranks the rest with weights <a class=\"cite\" href=\"references.html#r6\">[6]</a>. Set your own priorities and see who comes first.</p>\n  <div class=\"grid-2\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">\n    <div class=\"panel reveal\">\n      <h3>Your weights</h3>\n      <div class=\"seg presets\" id=\"presets\">\n        <button data-w=\"25,25,25,25\" class=\"on\">Equal</button>\n        <button data-w=\"15,55,15,15\">Cost</button>\n        <button data-w=\"15,15,15,55\">Community</button>\n        <button data-w=\"55,15,15,15\">Technology</button>\n      </div>\n      <div id=\"weightControls\"></div>\n      <p class=\"wsum\" id=\"wsum\"></p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"panel reveal\">\n      <h3>Who ranks first</h3>\n      <div class=\"bars\" id=\"rankBars\"></div>\n      <div class=\"verdict\" id=\"verdict\"></div>\n      <p class=\"note\" id=\"smaaNote\"></p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<!-- ============================ ECONOMICS =========================== -->\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"economics\">\n  <span class=\"kicker\">05 · The economics</span>\n  <h2>Timing, not chemistry, decides</h2>\n  <p class=\"lede\">Where the waste agency charges for disposal at hand-over, every cubic metre avoided saves the full charge. Where disposal is decades away, discounting erases the saving.</p>\n  <div class=\"grid-2\" style=\"margin-top:26px\">\n    <div class=\"panel reveal\">\n      <h3>Does licensing pay?</h3>\n      <div class=\"seg\" id=\"econCountry\"></div>\n      <div class=\"control\">\n        <label for=\"econVol\">Producer's liquid waste <output id=\"econVolOut\"></output></label>\n        <input type=\"range\" id=\"econVol\" min=\"0.1\" max=\"5\" step=\"0.1\" value=\"0.7\">\n      </div>\n      <svg class=\"econ-svg\" id=\"econSvg\" viewBox=\"0 0 560 150\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Volume against break-even\"></svg>\n      <div class=\"kpis\">\n        <div class=\"kpi\"><div class=\"v\" id=\"kSave\"></div><div class=\"l\">median saving per year</div></div>\n        <div class=\"kpi\"><div class=\"v\" id=\"kHead\"></div><div class=\"l\">volume it can lose and still pay</div></div>\n        <div class=\"kpi\"><div class=\"v\" id=\"kP\"></div><div class=\"l\">of 20,000 scenarios cheaper than cement</div></div>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"note\">Median saving per m³ and break-even volumes from our 20,000-draw Monte Carlo model; present values at a 3.5% real discount rate <a class=\"cite\" href=\"references.html#r10\">[10]</a>.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"panel reveal\">\n      <h3>Why distance kills value</h3>\n      <div class=\"control\">\n        <label for=\"years\">Years until the disposal charge is paid <output id=\"yearsOut\"></output></label>\n        <input type=\"range\" id=\"years\" min=\"0\" max=\"60\" step=\"1\" value=\"0\">\n      </div>\n      <svg class=\"econ-svg\" id=\"pvSvg\" viewBox=\"0 0 560 230\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Present value of A$1 avoided\"></svg>\n      <p id=\"pvText\" style=\"margin-top:10px\"></p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<!-- ============================== RISKS ============================= -->\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"risks\">\n  <span class=\"kicker\">06 · What could go wrong</span>\n  <h2>Sixteen risks, three that could stop everything</h2>\n  <p class=\"lede\">Agency refusal (R1), no operating licence for SyMo (R6) and a formulation that fails on real waste (R7) would remove both countries at once. They cannot be diversified, so each becomes a gate.</p>\n  <div class=\"seg\" id=\"riskMode\" style=\"margin:18px 0 18px\">\n    <button class=\"on\" data-m=\"inherent\">Before treatment</button>\n    <button data-m=\"residual\">After treatment</button>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"grid-2\">\n    <div class=\"panel reveal\">\n      <div class=\"matrix-wrap\">\n        <div class=\"axis-y\">Likelihood →</div>\n        <div class=\"matrix\" id=\"matrix\"></div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"axis-x\"><span>Low impact</span><span>Medium</span><span>High impact</span></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"panel risk-detail reveal\" id=\"riskDetail\"></div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n\n<!-- =============================== PLAN ============================= -->\n<section class=\"section\" id=\"plan\">\n  <span class=\"kicker\">07 · Our plan</span>\n  <h2>License, don't build</h2>\n  <p class=\"lede\">Offer COVRA a licence first and ONDRAF one in parallel, each priced on the disposal cost it avoids. Sign nothing until three gates are passed. Click a step.</p>\n  <div class=\"stepper\" id=\"stepper\"></div>\n  <div class=\"panel reveal\" id=\"stepDetail\"></div>\n  <h3 style=\"margin-top:44px\">What we ask ANSTO to do now</h3>\n  <div class=\"asks\">\n    <div class=\"ask\">Open characterisation and simulant-testing talks with COVRA, ONDRAF, Curium and IRE.</div>\n    <div class=\"ask\">Confirm the Petten waste volume; it has never been published.</div>\n    <div class=\"ask\">Consult host communities at Petten, Nieuwdorp, Fleurus and Dessel before any contract.</div>\n    <div class=\"ask\">Extend the cost model to South Africa's producer, NTP.</div>\n  </div>\n  <p class=\"note\"><b>Limitations.</b> Public documents only; no interviews with COVRA or ONDRAF. The Dutch volume is estimated. TRL 6 is provisional. Social licence evidence cannot yet compare sites.</p>\n</section>\n\n<footer class=\"footer\">\n  <span>SCPU3001 Interdisciplinary Impact · University of Sydney · Partner: ANSTO</span>\n  <span>Built in R and Quarto · <a href=\"references.html\">Sources [1]–[24]</a></span>\n</footer>\n\n<script src=\"assets/app.js\"></script>\n```\n",
